  "worked_solution": "The matrix $V$ is singular if and only if $det(V)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(V) & =7\\cdot y-5\\cdot y \\\\  & =7y-5y \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $y$ is $y=0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
